    "text": "This program only delivers gifts whose recipients are within distance D of Lapland (0,0). It loads each such gift and delivers it straight away, without moving the sleigh. It is a baseline: it ignores all gifts farther than D and uses no acceleration.\n\nThe output is always valid. Loading at the origin is within range, and delivery is within D of the child. No float or acceleration actions are needed. Distances are compared as integers (c\u00b2 + r\u00b2 \u2264 D\u00b2), which fits in `long long`.\n\n```cpp\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nint main(){\n    long long T,D,W,G;\n    cin>>T>>D>>W>>G;\n    for(int i=0;i<W;i++){long long l,a;cin>>l>>a;}\n    vector<string> out;\n    for(int i=0;i<G;i++){\n        string n;long long s,w,c,r;\n        cin>>n>>s>>w>>c>>r;\n        if(c*c+r*r<=D*D){\n            out.push_back(\"LoadGift \"+n);\n            out.push_back(\"DeliverGift \"+n);\n        }\n    }\n    printf(\"%d\\n\",(int)out.size());\n    for(auto&s:out)printf(\"%s\\n\",s.c_str());\n}\n```",
